  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1904.01 General Procedure for Establishing Protected Instream Flows",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1904.01 General Procedure for Establishing Protected Instream Flows. To establish protected instream flows on a designated river that conserve and protect the flow-dependent instream public uses and that meet applicable water quality standards:\n\n(a) The department shall:\n\n(1) Conduct a protected instream flow study and propose protected instream flows, as provided in Env-Wq 1904.02;\n\n(2) Publish the proposed protected instream flows in a proposed protected instream flow study report for public review, as provided in Env-Wq 1904.03; and\n\n(3) Hold a public hearing and receive comments on the study report and the proposed protected instream flows, as provided in Env-Wq 1904.04; and\n\n(b) The commissioner shall issue a decision establishing the protected instream flows for the designated river, as provided in Env-Wq 1904.05.\n\nSource. #7901, eff 5-29-03 (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1900) (formerly Env-Ws 1904.01); ss by #9936, eff 5-28-11; ss by #12695, eff 12-22-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1900.html"
